🎯 Steps to Apply
bash
# 1. Root folder mein .gitignore file banao (ye content paste karo)

# 2. Git ko batana hai ki naye ignore rules apply kare
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "chore: add .gitignore"

# 3. Agar pehle se kuch files galti se track ho gayi hain, unhe remove karo
git rm -r --cached node_modules venv .venv __pycache__ *.db 2>/dev/null

# 4. Phir push karo
git add .
git commit -m "chore: clean tracked files"
git push
⚠️ Important Notes
.env file kabhi push mat karo — isme API keys hoti hain

.env.example banao — ye template push karo, actual keys nahi

node_modules/ aur venv/ — ye bahut badi hoti hain, ignore zaroor karo

.db files — local database ignore karo

.gitkeep — empty folders ko track karne ke liye use hoti hai

📌 Bonus: .env.example File
Root folder ya backend/ mein .env.example banao:

env
# Gemini AI
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# JWT
SECRET_KEY=your_secret_key_here
ALGORITHM=HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60

# Database
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./audit_agent.db

# Uploads
UPLOAD_DIR=./uploads
MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE=10485760

# Server
HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=8000
DEBUG=True
